---

<DocsLayout
  title="Configuration"
  subtitle="How nikcli discovers, parses, merges, validates, and applies config across global, project, and runtime sources."
  description="Guide to nikcli configuration discovery, parsing, merging, validation, and per-environment overrides."
  toc={toc}
>
  <section id="overview" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>
      Config is resolved by <code>packages/nikcli/src/config/config.ts</code> with path discovery
      from <code>config/paths.ts</code>. Files are JSONC, support trailing commas, and are validated
      against <code>Config.Info</code>. Arrays for <code>plugin</code> and <code>instructions</code>
      are concatenated and deduplicated instead of simply replaced.
    </p>
    <div class="doc-grid not-prose">
      <DocCard title="Global config" eyebrow="User">
        <p>Loaded from <code>Global.Path.config/nikcli.json</code> and used for user-wide defaults.</p>
      </DocCard>
      <DocCard title="Project config" eyebrow="Repo">
        <p>Discovered upward from the working directory and worktree unless project config is disabled.</p>
      </DocCard>
      <DocCard title="Config directories" eyebrow="Plugins">
        <p>Directories ending in <code>.nikcli</code> and <code>NIKCLI_CONFIG_DIR</code> can provide config, commands, agents, modes, plugins, and instructions.</p>
      </DocCard>
      <DocCard title="Inline env config" eyebrow="Override">
        <p><code>NIKCLI_CONFIG_CONTENT</code> is merged after global/custom/project config, before directory extras are loaded.</p>
      </DocCard>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="resolution-order" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Resolution order</h2>
    <p>The current source order is precise and matters:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Remote well-known config from saved auth records with type <code>wellknown</code>. This is the lowest-precedence layer.</li>
      <li>Global config from <code>Global.Path.config/nikcli.json</code>.</li>
      <li>Custom config file from <code>NIKCLI_CONFIG</code>.</li>
      <li>Project config files discovered upward, unless <code>NIKCLI_DISABLE_PROJECT_CONFIG</code> is set.</li>
      <li>Inline JSON from <code>NIKCLI_CONFIG_CONTENT</code>.</li>
      <li>Config directories from <code>ConfigPaths.directories</code>, including global config dir, repo <code>.nikcli</code> dirs, home <code>.nikcli</code>, and <code>NIKCLI_CONFIG_DIR</code>.</li>
      <li>Command, agent, mode, and plugin entries loaded from those directories.</li>
      <li>Deprecated <code>mode</code> entries are migrated into <code>agent</code>.</li>
      <li><code>NIKCLI_PERMISSION</code> merges into <code>permission</code>.</li>
      <li>Legacy top-level <code>tools</code> is converted into permission rules.</li>
      <li>Runtime flag overrides such as <code>NIKCLI_DISABLE_AUTOCOMPACT</code> and <code>NIKCLI_DISABLE_PRUNE</code> are applied.</li>
    </ol>
    <DocCallout type="warn" title="Directory extras load after inline config">
      <p>
        Even though <code>NIKCLI_CONFIG_CONTENT</code> is the highest file/content layer, later
        directory scans still load command, agent, mode, plugin, and <code>.nikcli/nikcli.json</code>
        entries from config directories.
      </p>
    </DocCallout>
  </section>

  <section id="files" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Where files live</h2>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Location</th><th>How found</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Global config dir</td><td><code>Global.Path.config</code></td><td>User-wide <code>nikcli.json</code>, command, agent, plugin, and skill files.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Project config</td><td><code>Filesystem.findUp("nikcli.json")</code></td><td>Repo or subdirectory-specific overrides.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>.nikcli</code> directories</td><td><code>Filesystem.up</code> from directory/worktree and home</td><td>Local config modules and plugin entrypoints.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>NIKCLI_CONFIG</code></td><td>Exact env path</td><td>Single custom config file.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>NIKCLI_CONFIG_DIR</code></td><td>Exact env directory</td><td>Additional config directory, always included in directory scan.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <DocCode language="bash">
NIKCLI_CONFIG=/path/to/nikcli.json nikcli
NIKCLI_CONFIG_DIR=/path/to/.nikcli nikcli
NIKCLI_DISABLE_PROJECT_CONFIG=1 nikcli
    </DocCode>
  </section>

  <section id="tokens" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Config tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Config text supports <code>&#123;env:VAR&#125;</code> and <code>&#123;file:path&#125;</code>
      substitutions before JSONC parsing. Relative file paths resolve against the config file's
      directory. Lines commented with <code>//</code> skip file-token expansion.
    </p>
    <DocCode language="json" title="nikcli.json">
&#123;
  "provider": &#123;
    "openai": &#123;
      "options": &#123;
        "apiKey": "&#123;env:OPENAI_API_KEY&#125;"
      &#125;
    &#125;,
    "openrouter": &#123;
      "options": &#123;
        "apiKey": "&#123;file:./secrets/openrouter.txt&#125;"
      &#125;
    &#125;
  &#125;
&#125;
    </DocCode>
    <DocCallout type="info" title="Well-known config is safer">
      <p>
        Remote well-known config only receives the saved token through an explicitly named env key
        from the auth record. It does not freely read process env or local file references.
      </p>
    </DocCallout>
  </section>

  <section id="minimal" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Minimal config</h2>
    <DocCode language="json" title="nikcli.json">
&#123;
  "$schema": "https://nikcli-ai.dev/config.json",
  "theme": "tokyonight",
  "model": "openai/gpt-5",
  "small_model": "openai/gpt-5-mini",
  "default_agent": "build",
  "share": "manual",
  "provider": &#123;
    "openai": &#123;
      "options": &#123;
        "apiKey": "&#123;env:OPENAI_API_KEY&#125;"
      &#125;
    &#125;
  &#125;,
  "permission": &#123;
    "bash": "ask",
    "edit": "ask",
    "webfetch": "ask"
  &#125;
&#125;
    </DocCode>
  </section>

  <section id="top-level-fields" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Top-level fields</h2>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>$schema</code></td><td>Schema URL for editor validation.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>theme</code>, <code>locale</code>, <code>username</code></td><td>Presentation, language, regional formatting, and displayed user label.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>model</code>, <code>small_model</code></td><td>Default primary and helper model ids.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>default_agent</code>, <code>agent</code></td><td>Default agent and agent-specific prompts/tools/mode config.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>provider</code></td><td>Provider credentials, base URLs, models, variants, timeouts, allow/block lists.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>mcp</code>, <code>connectors</code></td><td>External tool servers and service connectors.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>formatter</code>, <code>lsp</code></td><td>Formatter and language server config or <code>false</code> to disable.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>permission</code>, <code>tools</code></td><td>Current permission rules and legacy tool boolean compatibility.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>plugin</code>, <code>instructions</code></td><td>Plugin specifiers and extra instruction files/patterns. Arrays concatenate across layers.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>server</code>, <code>remote</code></td><td>Serve/web defaults and remote control behavior.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>share</code>, <code>autoshare</code></td><td>Sharing mode. <code>autoshare</code> migrates to <code>share: auto</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>analytics</code></td><td>Anonymous usage reporting. On by default; see below to opt out.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>compaction</code></td><td>Auto compaction, prune, and reserved token buffer.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>experimental</code></td><td>Feature flags such as hooks, brain, memory, MCP timeout, native LLM runtime.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>image</code>, <code>attachment</code>, <code>speak</code></td><td>Media generation and attachment normalization config.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>notifications</code>, <code>mobile</code></td><td>Todo/general notifications and mobile development helpers.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="analytics" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Anonymous usage reporting</h2>
    <p>
      nikcli keeps per-day analytics locally, for the <code>/analytics</code> view. It also contributes those
      per-day totals, anonymously, to the public stats at <a href="/data">nikcli-ai.dev/data</a> — which is how
      that page can show the models people actually run on their own provider keys rather than only what the
      nikcli gateway served. <strong>This is on by default</strong>, because a sample of only the people who
      opted in would measure those people rather than the community.
    </p>
    <p>Turning it off, in order of precedence:</p>
    <pre class="doc-code"><code>{`# either environment variable, no config file needed
DO_NOT_TRACK=1
NIKCLI_DISABLE_ANALYTICS=1`}</code></pre>
    <pre class="doc-code"><code>{`{
  "analytics": {
    "share": false
  }
}`}</code></pre>
    <p>
      The environment variables win over the config, so a machine or a CI image can opt out without a config file
      existing at all.
    </p>
    <p>
      What is sent: date, provider, model, distinct session count, assistant message count, token counts and
      cost. Along with them goes a random UUID generated on your machine, so a resend replaces a day rather than
      doubling it — it is never published, and the public feed only ever emits a count of distinct installs.
    </p>
    <p>
      What is never sent: prompts, responses, file paths, repository names, session titles, account details, or
      anything about your environment. Set <code>analytics.endpoint</code> to send reports to your own collector
      instead of nikcli's. A failed report is retried later and never surfaces an error. Run
      <code>nikcli analytics show</code> to see exactly what would be sent.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="providers" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Providers</h2>
    <p>
      Provider entries are partial models.dev providers plus nikcli-specific options. Use
      <code>enabled_providers</code> to allow only specific provider ids, or
      <code>disabled_providers</code> to remove automatic providers.
    </p>
    <DocCode language="json" title="provider config">
&#123;
  "enabled_providers": ["openai", "anthropic", "openrouter"],
  "provider": &#123;
    "anthropic": &#123;
      "options": &#123;
        "apiKey": "&#123;env:ANTHROPIC_API_KEY&#125;"
      &#125;
    &#125;,
    "amazon-bedrock": &#123;
      "options": &#123;
        "region": "us-east-1",
        "profile": "default"
      &#125;
    &#125;
  &#125;
&#125;
    </DocCode>
  </section>

  <section id="agents-commands" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Agents and commands</h2>
    <p>
      <code>agent</code> config controls primary, subagent, and specialized agents. Deprecated
      <code>mode</code> entries are migrated into <code>agent</code> with <code>mode: primary</code>.
      Command templates are loaded from config and from config directories.
    </p>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>agent.build</code>, <code>agent.plan</code></td><td>Primary code and plan agents.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>agent.general</code>, <code>agent.explore</code>, <code>agent.scout</code></td><td>Subagent presets.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>agent.title</code>, <code>agent.summary</code>, <code>agent.compaction</code></td><td>Specialized helper agents.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>command</code></td><td>Named command templates available to CLI/TUI and prompt flows.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>instructions</code></td><td>Additional instruction files or globs included in session context.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="mcp-connectors" class="doc-section">
    <h2>MCP and connectors</h2>
    <DocCode language="json" title="external tools">
&#123;
  "mcp": &#123;
    "filesystem": &#123;
      "type": "local",
      "command": ["bunx", "@modelcontextprotocol/server-filesystem", "."]
    &#125;,
    "remote-docs": &#123;
      "type": "remote",
      "url": "https://example.com/mcp",
      "headers": &#123; "Authorization": "Bearer token" &#125;
    &#125;
  &#125;,
  "connectors": &#123;
    "github": &#123; "type": "github", "enabled": true &#125;,
    "slack": &#123; "type": "slack", "enabled": true &#125;,
    "figma": &#123; "type": "figma", "enabled": true &#125;
  &#125;
&#125;
    </DocCode>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Config</th><th>Valid forms</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>mcp.*</code></td><td>Local stdio command, remote URL with headers/OAuth, or enabled-only toggle patch.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>connectors.*</code></td><td>Figma, Slack, GitHub, Lovable, Discord, Teams, Google Chat, Linear, or enabled-only toggle patch.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="lsp-formatter" class="doc-section">
    <h2>LSP and formatter</h2>
    <p>
      <code>lsp</code> can be <code>false</code>, can disable a built-in server by id, or can define
      a custom server. Custom LSP servers must provide <code>extensions</code> unless they reuse a
      known built-in id. Formatter config follows the same pattern: disable all with
      <code>false</code>, override or disable named formatter entries otherwise.
    </p>
    <DocCode language="json" title="lsp config">
&#123;
  "lsp": &#123;
    "pyright": &#123; "disabled": true &#125;,
    "custom-ts": &#123;
      "command": ["typescript-language-server", "--stdio"],
      "extensions": [".ts", ".tsx"],
      "env": &#123; "NODE_ENV": "development" &#125;
    &#125;
  &#125;,
  "formatter": &#123;
    "prettier": &#123;
      "command": ["bunx", "prettier", "--write"],
      "extensions": [".ts", ".tsx", ".json"]
    &#125;
  &#125;
&#125;
    </DocCode>
  </section>

  <section id="permissions" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Permissions</h2>
    <p>
      Permission config accepts either a single action for all permissions, a tool-to-action map, or
      a tool-to-pattern map. Actions are <code>ask</code>, <code>allow</code>, and <code>deny</code>.
      The legacy top-level <code>tools</code> boolean map is converted into permission actions.
    </p>
    <DocCallout type="info" title="Permission modes">
      <p>
        TUI and mobile expose three named presets that map to the same <code>permission</code> map
        shape shown below: <code>require_approval</code> (every tool asks), <code>approve_for_me</code>
        (the empty-map default — trusted local work is allowed, shell/network/external/sensitive
        actions ask), and <code>full_access</code> (every tool is allowed). Editing individual tools
        after a preset switches the value to <code>custom</code>. See
        <a href="/docs/permissions">Permissions</a> for the full preset map and behavior table.
      </p>
    </DocCallout>
    <DocCode language="json" title="permission config">
&#123;
  "permission": &#123;
    "bash": &#123;
      "git status*": "allow",
      "rm *": "deny",
      "*": "ask"
    &#125;,
    "edit": "ask",
    "webfetch": "ask",
    "lsp": "ask"
  &#125;
&#125;
    </DocCode>
  </section>

  <section id="tui-keybinds" class="doc-section">
    <h2>TUI and keybinds</h2>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Behavior</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>tui.scroll_speed</code></td><td>Fixed scroll speed when scroll acceleration is disabled.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>tui.scroll_acceleration.enabled</code></td><td>Enable macOS-style scroll acceleration.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>tui.diff_style</code></td><td><code>auto</code> or <code>stacked</code> diff rendering.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>tui.mouse</code></td><td>Enable or disable mouse capture. Default is true.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>tui.sound</code></td><td>Enable ambient sound feedback.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>tui.bg_pulse</code></td><td>Enable animated home-logo background pulse.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>keybinds.command_list</code></td><td>Default <code>ctrl+p</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>keybinds.agent_cycle</code></td><td>Default <code>tab</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>keybinds.input_submit</code></td><td>Default <code>return</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>keybinds.input_newline</code></td><td>Default <code>shift+return,ctrl+return,alt+return,ctrl+j</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>keybinds.session_parent</code></td><td>Default <code>ctrl+b</code>, matching background/subagent parent behavior.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="notifications-mobile" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Notifications and mobile</h2>
    <p>
      Notification config is read by built-in notification plugins. Mobile config currently focuses
      on Tophat mobile project integration and defaults for platform/destination detection.
    </p>
    <DocCode language="json" title="notifications and mobile">
&#123;
  "notifications": &#123;
    "todo": &#123;
      "enabled": true,
      "slack": &#123; "enabled": true, "connector": "slack", "channel": "#builds" &#125;
    &#125;,
    "notify": &#123;
      "enabled": true,
      "events": &#123; "sessionIdle": true, "permissionAsked": true &#125;,
      "rateLimit": &#123; "windowMs": 60000, "maxPerWindow": 20 &#125;
    &#125;
  &#125;,
  "mobile": &#123;
    "tophat": &#123;
      "enabled": true,
      "defaultPlatform": "ios",
      "defaultDestination": "simulator"
    &#125;
  &#125;
&#125;
    </DocCode>
  </section>

  <section id="env-flags" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Environment flags</h2>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Flag</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>NIKCLI_CONFIG</code></td><td>Load an explicit config file after global config.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>NIKCLI_CONFIG_CONTENT</code></td><td>Merge inline JSON after project config.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>NIKCLI_CONFIG_DIR</code></td><td>Add a config directory to directory scanning.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>NIKCLI_DISABLE_PROJECT_CONFIG</code></td><td>Disable project-level file discovery and <code>.nikcli</code> project directories.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>NIKCLI_PERMISSION</code></td><td>Inline permission overrides.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>NIKCLI_DISABLE_DEFAULT_PLUGINS</code></td><td>Skip built-in external plugins.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>NIKCLI_DISABLE_EXTERNAL_SKILLS</code></td><td>Disable external skill discovery.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>NIKCLI_DISABLE_LSP_DOWNLOAD</code></td><td>Prevent automatic LSP server downloads.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>NIKCLI_ENABLE_EXPERIMENTAL_MODELS</code></td><td>Keep alpha models in provider catalog.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>NIKCLI_DISABLE_AUTOCOMPACT</code></td><td>Force <code>compaction.auto</code> false.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>NIKCLI_DISABLE_PRUNE</code></td><td>Force <code>compaction.prune</code> false.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>NIKCLI_SERVER_PASSWORD</code></td><td>Enable Basic Auth for server mode.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>NIKCLI_SERVER_TAILSCALE_AUTH</code></td><td>Trust loopback Tailscale identity headers.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>NIKCLI_EXPERIMENTAL_HTTPAPI</code></td><td>Enable typed HttpApi bridge.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>NIKCLI_EXPERIMENTAL_LSP_TOOL</code></td><td>Enable the LSP tool in the registry.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>NIKCLI_EXPERIMENTAL_LSP_TY</code></td><td>Use ty and disable pyright in the built-in LSP set.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="failure-modes" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Failure modes</h2>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Likely cause</th><th>Fix</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Config parse error includes JSONC input</td><td>Syntax error after token substitution.</td><td>Check the reported line/column and any <code>&#123;file:*&#125;</code> expansion.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Project config ignored</td><td><code>NIKCLI_DISABLE_PROJECT_CONFIG</code> is set.</td><td>Unset the flag or use <code>NIKCLI_CONFIG</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Custom LSP rejected</td><td>Unknown LSP id has no <code>extensions</code>.</td><td>Add the extension list or use a known built-in id.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Plugin duplicated</td><td>Multiple layers append plugin arrays.</td><td>Config loader deduplicates plugin specs, but check versioned specs and force install behavior.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Permission does not match</td><td>Later rules or stored always approvals override earlier ones.</td><td>Check merge order and project permission storage.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="source-anchors" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Source anchors</h2>
    <table class="doc-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Need</th><th>File</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Config loading and schema</td><td><code>packages/nikcli/src/config/config.ts</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Config path discovery</td><td><code>packages/nikcli/src/config/paths.ts</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>TUI config</td><td><code>packages/nikcli/src/config/tui.ts</code>, <code>packages/nikcli/src/config/tui-schema.ts</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Environment flags</td><td><code>@nikcli-ai/util/flag</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Global paths</td><td><code>@nikcli-ai/util/global</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Plugin install config patching</td><td><code>packages/nikcli/src/plugin/installer.ts</code></td></tr>
